# Keep Windows scripts byte-exact.
#
# git normally stores text blobs with LF and converts on checkout. That is
# wrong for .bat/.cmd: cmd.exe can misparse an LF-only batch file (multi-line
# if blocks and for /f loops are the known trouble spots), and
# raw.githubusercontent.com always serves the blob, so a user who downloads
# the script straight from GitHub would get the LF version.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so the CRLF bytes are stored
# as-is and every download path delivers the same file that was tested.
*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text

# Same for the shipped readme: keep the UTF-8 BOM and CRLF exactly as written,
# because it is opened in Windows Notepad by non-technical users.
使用前必讀.txt -text
